Express Adapter > Basic Setup > Behind a proxy

Rate limits and the per-IP budget use `req.ip`. Behind a reverse proxy or a load balancer, `req.ip` is the proxy's address unless you tell Express to trust it, and then every visitor shares one limit. With one proxy in front:

```typescript
import express from 'express';

const app = express();
app.set('trust proxy', 1);
```

The server logs a warning when requests carry `X-Forwarded-For` but `trust proxy` is off. Don't set it to `true` unless every request comes through your proxy: Express would then believe any `X-Forwarded-For` a visitor sends.

AI Providers > Tool support

All providers support tool calling with one tool format. ChatCops converts tool definitions to each provider's native format:

- Claude: `tools` array with `input_schema`
- OpenAI: `tools` array with `function.parameters`
- Gemini: `functionDeclarations` with `parametersJsonSchema`

When the model calls several tools at once, they run in parallel on every provider.

```typescript
import { LeadCaptureTool } from '@chatcops/core';
import { chatcopsMiddleware } from '@chatcops/server';

const saveLead = async (lead: { name: string; email: string }) => console.log(lead);
chatcopsMiddleware({
  provider: { type: 'claude', apiKey: '...' },
  systemPrompt: '...',
  tools: [new LeadCaptureTool(saveLead)],
});
```

The same tool definition works across all providers without changes.

Next.js, Hono, Bun and Deno > Bun

```typescript
import { chatcopsVercelHandler } from '@chatcops/server';

const chat = chatcopsVercelHandler({
  provider: {
    type: 'claude',
    apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY!,
  },
  systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful assistant.',
  allowedOrigins: ['*'],
  sessionSecrets: [process.env.CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET!],
  // Set below from the socket, so a visitor can't choose it.
  clientIp: (req) => req.headers.get('x-client-ip'),
});

Bun.serve({
  port: 3000,
  // Replies stream for a while; Bun closes idle connections after 10 seconds by default.
  idleTimeout: 120,
  fetch(req, server) {
    const { pathname } = new URL(req.url);
    if (pathname !== '/api/chat' && pathname !== '/api/chat/session') return new Response('Not found', { status: 404 });

    // The visitor's IP, for per-IP rate limits and budgets. set() replaces
    // any x-client-ip the visitor sent.
    const headers = new Headers(req.headers);
    headers.set('x-client-ip', server.requestIP(req)?.address ?? '');
    return chat(new Request(req, { headers }));
  },
});
```

Knowledge Base > Custom Knowledge Source

Implement `KnowledgeSource` for database-backed or vector search:

```typescript
import type { KnowledgeSource } from '@chatcops/core';

const vectorDB = { async search(_query: string, _options: { topK: number }) { return [] as Array<{ text: string }>; } };

class VectorKnowledgeSource implements KnowledgeSource {
  type = 'vector';

  async getContext(query: string): Promise<string> {
    const results = await vectorDB.search(query, { topK: 5 });
    return results.map(r => r.text).join('\n\n');
  }
}
